---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PricingCards from "../components/PricingCards.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Pricing — Rotagivan"
  description="Rotagivan is free to download. Voice mode is an optional paid add-on."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">PRICING</p>
      <h1>
        Free to download.
        <br />
        <em>Voice when you want it.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The launcher, Window Manager, macros, gestures and sync are free. Voice
        mode is the one paid feature.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-label="Plans">
      <PricingCards />
    </section>
    <section class="faq">
      <p class="eyebrow">A FEW THINGS TO KNOW</p>
      <h2>Before your next move.</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>What do I get for free?</summary>
        <p>
          Everything except Voice mode: the radial HUD, Window Manager, Chrome
          tabs and Recent Apps HUDs, macros and keybindings, profiles and
          layers, per-app overrides, ZSA Navigator gestures and tuning, and
          settings sync.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How does Voice mode work?</summary>
        <p>
          Start voice from the HUD or its hotkey and say a short command.
          Rotagivan transcribes it with your configured provider (OpenAI, or
          OpenRouter/xAI), ranks your own registered actions, and shows the top
          three. Nothing runs until you confirm. Voice mode uses your own API
          key, so provider usage is billed by that provider.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do I unlock Voice mode after paying?</summary>
        <p>
          Checkout is handled securely by Stripe. Afterwards you get a license
          key; paste it into Rotagivan to unlock Voice mode on up to three of
          your Macs. The app re-checks the license periodically and keeps
          working offline in between.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need a ZSA Navigator?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Every HUD and action can be reached with keyboard hotkeys. The
          app is built around ZSA Navigator touch input, and Apple trackpad
          gesture actions are available experimentally.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is the website demo the full app?</summary>
        <p>
          No. The demo simulates a handful of workflows inside your browser.
          The Mac app connects actions to your real apps and inputs once you
          grant the macOS permissions it asks for.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
